          "title": "You'll want to know: தொடை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தொடை — toṭai — \"a thigh\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஓடும்போது என் தொடையில் வலி வந்தது. ōṭumpōtu eṉ toṭaiyil vali vantatu. While running I got a pain in my thigh."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தொடை (toṭai) and தொடு \"to touch\" are different words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தொடை (toṭai) is native Dravidian (DEDR 3302); the entry also gives the form துடை tuṭai."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
